Z||000000||sluppy123||01-24-2001||10:21 PM||||Here's some pictures of the interior in my 87 GT. My headliner was begining to sag so I recovered it with some Med Grey vinyl. It matches my Leather seats perfectly. (the pictures aren't the greatest, still learning how to run my digital camera)<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=39036605&Sequence=0"> <P>While I was at it I also recovered the fire wall panel with the came vinyl.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=39036488&Sequence=0"> <P>Mr. Mikes leather seats.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=11172186&p=39042962&Sequence=0"> <P><P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||01-24-2001||11:15 PM||||Looks Good!!!!<P>Sluppy, Did you use any padding for the headliner?? also what type of glue did you use?? Love those seats. I'm still working on my interior. I need the headliner and dash cover, and yes....I need those seats you got.<BR>I posted pics a while back of the center console, door panels and gauge pods, I just need to get the time to finish.<BR>Good looking job!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD<P>||||reg||14
